WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.898
In the previous video, you saw&nbsp;us getting ready for this year.

00:00:04.898 --> 00:00:08.650
Cleaning everything, installing the office, setting up tents...

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:12.578
Because, people are arriving to help out, 
with the next season of Project Kamp.

00:00:13.863 --> 00:00:19.338
So, here we&nbsp;are: new year, new projects, new people,
 new leaves, new flowers, same old sweater!

00:00:19.838 --> 00:00:23.061
In this video, I'm&nbsp;going to show you all the things
 we're going to do this year.

00:00:23.061 --> 00:00:26.015
And, we're going to start off&nbsp;with our construction projects.

00:00:26.015 --> 00:00:26.776
Let me show you!

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.990
So, on the land, we have the small ruin,
 which -&nbsp;last year - we renovated.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:37.671
So, we added the roof on top, insulation, 
made it into a dry space...

00:00:38.144 --> 00:00:39.674
Built a veranda outside...

00:00:39.674 --> 00:00:42.480
Because, the goal is to build a guest house in here.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.616
But, actually, for the coming season, 
we don't really need that yet...

00:00:45.616 --> 00:00:47.557
So, we're going&nbsp;to use it for something else!

00:00:47.557 --> 00:00:48.386
Let me show you!

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.335
So, this year, we're going to use this space as an&nbsp;office.

00:00:54.335 --> 00:00:59.375
So, we can do very productive work, 
insulated from the heat, and the cold.

00:00:59.375 --> 00:01:02.692
I cannot go further,&nbsp;because no shoes
 are allowed after this point...

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:06.111
So, this is a good office...

00:01:06.111 --> 00:01:07.677
We're going to keep it&nbsp;for that.

00:01:07.677 --> 00:01:12.547
One thing we still want to do here, this year, 
is this box here, which is still unfinished...

00:01:12.547 --> 00:01:15.859
So, as you can see: raw floor, insulation material...

00:01:15.859 --> 00:01:19.695
Because, this is going to be the shower, 
and the&nbsp;toilet, for the future guest house.

00:01:19.695 --> 00:01:21.606
And, we're gonna renovate that this year...

00:01:21.832 --> 00:01:23.921
So, that's on the to-do&nbsp;list.

00:01:23.921 --> 00:01:26.120
And, something else for this ruin is outside..

00:01:31.017 --> 00:01:32.945
So, here we are in the bottom of the ruin

00:01:33.644 --> 00:01:36.605
It's a&nbsp;bit older building, made from old granite rocks.

00:01:36.605 --> 00:01:38.448
Currently used as a storage...

00:01:38.448 --> 00:01:40.678
I want to renovate&nbsp;this room this year.

00:01:40.678 --> 00:01:45.920
But, we noticed in the winter that this wall was getting 
completely wet, and made&nbsp;the floor wet...

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.388
So, we need to fix that, before we're going to renovate it.

00:01:49.388 --> 00:01:51.460
But, yeah, there are two rooms&nbsp;underneath the ruin.

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:55.171
And, this year, we want to make sure they're waterproof
and cleaned up, so we can use&nbsp;them.

00:01:55.603 --> 00:01:58.484
So, that was all the renovations we're going to do for the ruin.

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:01.115
It's almost there already, so, we just need to wrap it up...

00:02:01.115 --> 00:02:05.719
And, next, let me show you the other 
renovation project we're going&nbsp;to do...

00:02:05.719 --> 00:02:08.040
Which is involving a shipping container.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:19.641
So, here we have a beautiful, new, old, 
rusty&nbsp;shipping container...

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.669
We got another one this winter...

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:32.677
They're very good, if you want a quick, temporary,&nbsp;dry structure...

00:02:33.232 --> 00:02:37.335
So, we already have two shipping&nbsp;containers, 
and this one is going to be storage.&nbsp;

00:02:37.335 --> 00:02:42.780
So, there we're going to put all things, like bulk food
for the kitchen, seasonal tents, some garden tools...

00:02:43.171 --> 00:02:45.078
And, we're going to build a big roof on top!

00:02:45.078 --> 00:02:47.623
The&nbsp;biggest roof we have so far in Project Kamp!

00:02:47.623 --> 00:02:51.426
So, we can also store other things, 
like our material&nbsp;storage on the outside.

00:02:52.126 --> 00:02:55.112
This is going to be one big container!

00:02:56.799 --> 00:03:01.845
So, currently, we all live in vans and tents in Basekamp,
 which is a pretty good setup.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:06.898
And, we also have this old, yellow post office van,
which we're going to renovate this year.

00:03:06.898 --> 00:03:08.460
Because, it's been here two years...

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.746
It's got a&nbsp;few leaks, a bit rough inside...

00:03:10.746 --> 00:03:15.474
So, we're gonna clean it all up, and build a 
nice proper space in there, so visitors can stay.

00:03:16.194 --> 00:03:18.897
And, yeah, like, all of us live in vans and tents.

00:03:18.897 --> 00:03:21.124
And, it's cool, but&nbsp;it's very temporary!

00:03:21.124 --> 00:03:24.556
So, this year, for the first time: 
we're going to build our Level 2 house!

00:03:24.865 --> 00:03:25.856
The&nbsp;first one.

00:03:25.856 --> 00:03:27.420
And, let me explain what that means...

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.789
So, these are what we call Level 1 houses.

00:03:33.789 --> 00:03:35.421
This, and also, vans...

00:03:35.421 --> 00:03:37.573
Temporary structures that you put somewhere...

00:03:37.573 --> 00:03:38.959
You can take them down.

00:03:38.959 --> 00:03:42.112
For mostly to stay in the season,
and not really in the winter...

00:03:42.112 --> 00:03:44.638
It doesn't require any legal paperwork...

00:03:44.638 --> 00:03:46.746
You&nbsp;just plop them there, and you can stay in it.

00:03:47.055 --> 00:03:49.619
So, yeah, Level 1 houses, we have a lot of that.

00:03:49.619 --> 00:03:51.530
But now, we're going for a Level 2 house.

00:03:53.381 --> 00:03:57.231
So, a Level 2 house doesn't exist yet, 
but just to&nbsp;illustrate what it could look like...

00:03:57.622 --> 00:03:59.889
Something like a shipping container...

00:03:59.889 --> 00:04:04.135
Not even as complex as this&nbsp;one, 
but really just a container, that you put on a piece of land...

00:04:04.135 --> 00:04:09.048
And then, you can live in it, which&nbsp;gives more comfort, 
than something like a van, or a tent...

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:12.640
But, it's not as complex as legalizing&nbsp;an entire new house... 

00:04:13.134 --> 00:04:15.042
So, that's what we consider a Level 2 house.

00:04:15.042 --> 00:04:19.463
This sort of in-between&nbsp;state, 
that is still temporary, but gives you more comfort.

00:04:19.936 --> 00:04:24.293
And, just while we're at it, let me also&nbsp;explain you 
what we think is a Level 3 house...

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.207
So, a Level 3 house would be more something&nbsp;like this!

00:04:28.207 --> 00:04:34.055
It requires a bit of imagination, but the principle would be
 a proper house, built with&nbsp;heavy stones.

00:04:34.055 --> 00:04:38.497
Legalized in the paperwork, where someone can 
really live properly all year round.

00:04:38.497 --> 00:04:43.824
We're not there yet, but in the future, for sure, 
we would have these kind of houses as well here in&nbsp;the project.

00:04:44.091 --> 00:04:46.076
And, that's what we consider a Level 3 house.

00:04:46.426 --> 00:04:47.448
A small disclaimer.

00:04:47.448 --> 00:04:50.680
The things, Level&nbsp;1, 2, and 3 house, we made them up...

00:04:51.297 --> 00:04:56.117
It's just for ourselves internally, that we know how to build,
and develop each type of housing.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:58.763
But, for now, no Level 3 house yet...

00:04:58.763 --> 00:05:01.122
We're going to start this year, 
with&nbsp;our first Level 2 house.

00:05:01.122 --> 00:05:03.600
Which is probably going to be built on a trailer.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:06.484
A big trailer, with the size of&nbsp;a shipping container.

00:05:06.484 --> 00:05:08.987
Not sure yet, if it's going to be shipping container house...

00:05:08.987 --> 00:05:12.920
Anyway, our next renovation&nbsp;project is gonna be our big ruin.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:27.156
So, here we are in the big ruin, 
or what we call&nbsp;our Community Center.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:29.410
We're a bit behind with this project...

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:34.157
We hoped we would do more, but most of&nbsp;the last year,  
we spent on designing.

00:05:34.747 --> 00:05:38.057
So, just to give you an imagination, what it's going to be like...

00:05:38.057 --> 00:05:43.716
This building is going to be the kitchen,
where you can do big shared meals for the community.

00:05:44.477 --> 00:05:49.654
In this&nbsp;area, here is going to be more like toilets and shower,
where the people can clean up.

00:05:50.559 --> 00:05:54.562
And, over here, the big space is going to be a shared community space.

00:05:54.562 --> 00:05:59.163
So, when it's hot outside or cold and rainy,
you can be in here sheltered.

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:03.597
And, we would also have a few offices, 
where people can do digital&nbsp;work.

00:06:03.926 --> 00:06:08.203
So, online with the help of some others, 
we started making the drawings of this building.

00:06:08.738 --> 00:06:12.640
But, the next step is actually to look into the legalization of it...

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:16.110
Because, we want to keep as&nbsp;much of the existing structure as possible. 

00:06:16.254 --> 00:06:19.766
Which is, obviously, not really the usual thing to do...

00:06:19.992 --> 00:06:22.130
And, so, we're not sure how much is possible...

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:24.000
We need to look into the fire regulations...

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:26.039
And, there's a bit&nbsp;of an urgency here...

00:06:26.039 --> 00:06:29.917
Because, the local rules and regulations change every 10 years.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:35.495
And, this is the&nbsp;year they're going to change, and they might change a lot,
because there was a fire here a few years&nbsp;ago.

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:37.370
So, yeah, we're in the middle of that process...

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:43.640
You can follow it on the research module, 
but it's&nbsp;still a bit in the boring process of legalization...

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:45.922
So, those were the construction projects...

00:06:45.922 --> 00:06:48.667
And&nbsp;next, let me show you our landscaping projects.

00:06:50.551 --> 00:06:53.097
And, this category is a bit overwhelming

00:06:53.097 --> 00:06:56.098
Because, if you have 10 hectares of land, 
there's so much to do...

00:06:56.098 --> 00:06:57.389
You can grow your own food...

00:06:57.780 --> 00:06:58.971
Plant&nbsp;a forest...

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:00.864
Make swales, retain the water...

00:07:00.864 --> 00:07:02.160
 

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:04.051
So, it's important to prioritize.

00:07:04.195 --> 00:07:08.388
And, last year, it became pretty clear to us, 
what should be our first priority.

00:07:08.655 --> 00:07:11.015
It's a bit lame, but kind&nbsp;of essential...

00:07:11.015 --> 00:07:15.004
It's to make sure we're more fire resilient, 
because the land burned down, a&nbsp;few years ago.

00:07:15.107 --> 00:07:16.671
The region always burns down...

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:20.788
So, especially in the summer, it's kind of important to&nbsp;be fire resilient...

00:07:20.788 --> 00:07:24.511
Because, otherwise, the whole operation just wipes down in an afternoon...

00:07:25.992 --> 00:07:28.657
So, that's kind of where we based our landscape goals upon...

00:07:28.657 --> 00:07:32.985
And, one of the main things we're&nbsp;going to do,
 is to clear more of the native trees.

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:34.464
Which, we've done for instance here...

00:07:34.464 --> 00:07:35.894
There used to&nbsp;be a lot of bushes around.

00:07:36.367 --> 00:07:38.626
Then, we cleared it up so the native trees can grow.

00:07:38.626 --> 00:07:41.819
And, they are a&nbsp;bit more fire resilient than the other ones.

00:07:42.292 --> 00:07:44.339
But, there's still a lot to do...

00:07:44.339 --> 00:07:46.867
And, so, as you can&nbsp;see, this is what it usually looks like.

00:07:47.422 --> 00:07:50.376
Just a lot of bushes and vegetation...

00:07:50.376 --> 00:07:56.995
Which, is usually&nbsp;a good thing, but here especially, 
on our rocky hill area, it's bordering the neighbors' land.

00:07:56.995 --> 00:08:02.171
Which has an eucalyptus farm, so, 
it's the highest risk of fire up here!

00:08:02.171 --> 00:08:05.903
So, we want to make sure,&nbsp;that this area is a bit more fire resilient.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:19.725
So, our next project is this lake right here.

00:08:20.178 --> 00:08:21.486
I guess, I should watch my words...

00:08:21.486 --> 00:08:26.015
According to the YouTube comments, 
this is a swamp, or a pond, but not a&nbsp;lake...

00:08:26.015 --> 00:08:27.997
Makes sense, but it's pretty cool!

00:08:27.997 --> 00:08:32.016
It's for animals, where they can drink,
and for us, to have&nbsp;a bit of a water reservoir.

00:08:32.222 --> 00:08:36.878
However, it needs a bit of clearing up, 
because the soil around it is&nbsp;eroding...

00:08:37.125 --> 00:08:38.751
And, we also want to make it bigger...

00:08:38.916 --> 00:08:42.067
The main reason for that is so we have a bigger water&nbsp;reservoir.

00:08:42.067 --> 00:08:47.424
So, in case of a fire, or a very dry summer, 
we can retain more water, as a backup.

00:08:47.835 --> 00:08:52.300
The&nbsp;neighbors actually also told us that there used to be helicopters here,
 when there's a fire to take&nbsp;the water.

00:08:52.773 --> 00:08:55.257
Which they currently can't do, because it's fully overgrown...

00:08:55.381 --> 00:08:57.719
So, if we clean it up a bit, they&nbsp;could.

00:08:57.719 --> 00:09:00.428
So, yeah, we want to revitalize this water reservoir.

00:09:00.428 --> 00:09:03.332
Also to make sure the water from the land&nbsp;flows in here...

00:09:03.434 --> 00:09:06.991
It retains as a healthy place for the animals to come...

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:12.000
We could actually use some&nbsp;help here, from someone 
that has more expertise in building lakes, swamps, ponds...

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:13.240
Whatever you want&nbsp;to call this...

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:15.375
If you want to come, and help out, let us know!

00:09:15.375 --> 00:09:16.477
Sign up on the website!

00:09:16.971 --> 00:09:20.608
So we can make&nbsp;this into a nice, little, thriving ecosystem.

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:28.938
So, sorry YouTube...

00:09:28.938 --> 00:09:31.297
This year, we're still not going to grow our own food.

00:09:31.297 --> 00:09:35.898
We just don't have the capacity yet, 
but one thing we do want to do, is plant more fruit trees.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:39.056
We&nbsp;already did this a bit here and there..

00:09:39.056 --> 00:09:41.840
But, this year, we really want to plant between a 50 and&nbsp;100...

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:45.166
Mainly because it's more of a long-term investment,
to grow our own foods.

00:09:45.166 --> 00:09:48.735
That in many&nbsp;years from now, we can pick the fruits.

00:09:49.599 --> 00:09:51.100
So, yeah, planting fruit trees this year.

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:54.656
Another thing, we&nbsp;want to do this year, is cleaning the creek.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:57.847
We actually already wanted to do this last year, and we started.

00:09:57.847 --> 00:10:02.381
but it became a bit more work than planned so we were not able to finish it

00:10:02.381 --> 00:10:06.000
But, the principle would be: we have this creek flowing on the land...

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.982
And, we want to make sure&nbsp;to remove all the invasive species there.

00:10:08.982 --> 00:10:13.618
And, keep the native trees, so they can really grow, 
and flourish, and create a healthy place.

00:10:20.391 --> 00:10:23.202
So, here we are at the waterfall, 
which is&nbsp;flowing right there...

00:10:23.202 --> 00:10:26.638
Water going down, and this is the lagoon we cleaned up last year.

00:10:26.638 --> 00:10:30.219
It's now in the winter, so it filled up with water, which is really cool!

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.976
But, it's actually not&nbsp;that deep...

00:10:32.976 --> 00:10:36.449
It looks like a lot of water, but it's only this deep...

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:41.947
And, there's just this&nbsp;thick layer of leaves, soil, earth in there...

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:46.167
So, this year, we want to clean it us,
so it's a&nbsp;nicer place to swim.

00:10:46.464 --> 00:10:51.227
But also, just so we have a bigger water capacity storage here.

00:10:51.227 --> 00:10:55.739
And the&nbsp;soil that we're going to take out is very good, 
 but we're going to put it around&nbsp;this area.

00:10:55.739 --> 00:10:59.622
So, the things can grow more there, 
and we can store more water in here...

00:10:59.622 --> 00:11:01.500
So, it's going to be a big muddy job in here!

00:11:08.324 --> 00:11:13.170
And, besides all of the landscaping work, 
we&nbsp;also have a few upgrades we need to make to Basekamp...

00:11:13.664 --> 00:11:19.620
One of them is a roof here, because now, 
if&nbsp;it rains and the door is open, it always gets wet...&nbsp;

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:20.930
The pans, it's not nice...

00:11:21.197 --> 00:11:24.394
And, it's also when the sun&nbsp;shines, 
it's very hot, when you're cooking...

00:11:24.394 --> 00:11:25.577
So, we're going to make a little roof there.

00:11:26.132 --> 00:11:28.789
And, besides that, this year we also want to be with more people.

00:11:28.789 --> 00:11:30.694
So, last year we were at a maximum of 15.

00:11:30.694 --> 00:11:34.891
This year, we're&nbsp;going for 25, 
which means we also need to upgrade a few systems.

00:11:34.891 --> 00:11:36.860
So, for instance, how we do dishwashing...

00:11:37.148 --> 00:11:38.711
It's a bit messy where you store the plates...

00:11:38.711 --> 00:11:43.683
So, we're going to upgrade that as well, so,
 we have&nbsp;a few Basekamp improvements we have to make...

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:48.955
Which means, we also need to upgrade our toilet...

00:11:49.346 --> 00:11:52.966
Now, this toilet is still the exact same one, 
as how we originally built it!

00:11:53.192 --> 00:11:58.590
We even have this little&nbsp;sign, that says you need 
to add some sawdust after pooping, from cardboard!

00:11:58.981 --> 00:12:00.270
Still alive, still&nbsp;there!

00:12:00.270 --> 00:12:02.731
Everything else got moldy, except this thing...

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:05.224
So, the toilet itself is kind of okay...

00:12:05.224 --> 00:12:08.698
It doesn't&nbsp;really need upgrades, but we just need another toilet...

00:12:08.698 --> 00:12:10.078
Because, we're going to be more people...

00:12:10.078 --> 00:12:14.603
So, in the morning, when it's busy, 
some people have a high needency to go.

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:17.467
We just need a second&nbsp;toilet, 
so we're going to build that.

00:12:17.467 --> 00:12:21.694
And, probably, this time different, 
where we separate the urine&nbsp;from the poop.

00:12:23.586 --> 00:12:24.744
And, finally, here we are...

00:12:24.744 --> 00:12:27.788
Back in the office, because we're gonna 
have a few things&nbsp;different for the coming year...

00:12:28.364 --> 00:12:29.529
A few positions open...

00:12:29.632 --> 00:12:35.356
One, is that there can be a Web Developer&nbsp;in-house here,
 so we can improve our software to share our documentation.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:40.672
And, also, a position for a&nbsp;Communication Manager, 
that helps us to distribute our messages in the world.

00:12:41.412 --> 00:12:43.535
And finally, we also&nbsp;upgraded our video team!

00:12:43.535 --> 00:12:46.295
Before, we had Javi, and now we also have Guilherme here.

00:12:47.138 --> 00:12:50.087
And, I think I just&nbsp;pronounced his name wrong -- it's a difficult name...

00:12:50.940 --> 00:12:53.382
But, uh, we can call him Guy!

00:12:53.382 --> 00:12:54.183
- Hi YouTube!

00:12:54.409 --> 00:12:58.604
Their goal is to get the YouTube subscribers to 1.000.000 this year!

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:02.542
And, that's a hundred thousand, so we have some work to do...

00:13:03.180 --> 00:13:06.752
They're now editing the video for next week, 
which is going to be about&nbsp;the pickup.

00:13:06.752 --> 00:13:09.784
If you already want to see that, make sure to support on Patreon.

00:13:10.113 --> 00:13:13.590
Or not, and you'll see&nbsp;it next week, here on YouTube!

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:14.460
It's gonna be cool!

